{"symbol":"AIRFLOA","yahoo":"AIRFLOA.BO","bse":null,"isin":null,"sme":null,"name":"Airfloa Rail Technology Limited","sector":"Industrials","industry":"Railroads","website":"https://www.airflow.co.in","about":"Airfloa Rail Technology Limited engages in the design, development, analysis, fabrication, machining, and assembly of composite parts for railway vehicles and transportation. It offers rail car body parts, such as exterior sidewalls, end walls, roofs, end roofs, and nose cones; rail interior parts, including doors, windows, seats, luggage racks and partitions, handrails, flooring paneling, aluminum composites, fiber reinforced plastics (FRP) and stainless-steel panels, LED lighting systems, and PAS and cyclonic air filters, as well as heating, ventilating and air conditioning systems; and composites comprising FRP interior panels and modular toilets. The company also provides AMCA ground simulators and precusion machining tools for aerospace; and artillery tank bodies and body armor for defense applications. In addition, it undertakes interior furnishing projects for Indian Railways and provides consultation services for transportation. Further, it offers high-precision forged and machined rolling stock components, rail coach exterior and interior systems such as sidewalls, end walls, roofs, nose cones, doors, windows, seats, luggage racks, panels, toilets, lighting systems, and HVAC interfaces, as well as composite structures. The company was incorporated in 1998 and is based in Chennai, India.","updated":"2026-10-03T11:12:49+00:00","quote":{"price":520.2,"prevClose":528.35,"marketCap":1246.92,"high52":593.85,"low52":246.0,"pe":27.89,"bookValue":99.77,"dividendRate":0.0,"roe":22.27,"shares":2.397,"insiders":70.18,"institutions":0.0},"prices":{"dates":["2025-09-18","2025-09-19","2025-09-22","2025-09-23","2025-09-24","2025-09-25","2025-09-26","2025-09-29","2025-09-30","2025-10-01","2025-10-03","2025-10-06","2025-10-07","2025-10-08","2025-10-09","2025-10-10","202